#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Obtain samples from an ansatz {#obtain-samples-from-an-ansatz}"
msgstr ""
"Kumuha ng mga sample mula sa isang ansatz {#obtain-samples-from-an-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once the molecule information has been loaded in, you should specify an "
"ansatz circuit and optimize it for execution. This involves considering any "
"symmetries of your problem, the choice of ansatz, and optimize it to run on "
"quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag na-load na ang impormasyon ng molecule, dapat kang magtukoy ng isang "
"ansatz circuit at i-optimize ito para sa pagpapatupad. Kasama dito ang "
"pagsasaalang-alang sa anumang mga symmetry ng iyong problema, ang pagpili ng"
" ansatz, at pag-optimize nito upang tumakbo sa quantum hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, these choices are problem specific and out of scope for this guide."
" Instead, to demonstrate the SQD workflow, we will generate a random set of "
"counts for the configuration recovery loop to post-process. This simulates "
"the measurement data of a 32-qubit circuit sampled with 10,000 shots. After "
"the count data has been generated, the `recover_configurations()` method "
"requires that you convert the count data into a matrix of the bitstrings "
"measured at each shot, as well as an array of probabilities for each state "
"that was measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, ang mga pagpiling ito ay tiyak sa problema at labas sa saklaw ng"
" gabay na ito. Sa halip, upang ipakita ang SQD workflow, gagawa tayo ng "
"random na hanay ng mga count para sa configuration recovery loop na i-post-"
"process. Sinisimulate nito ang measurement data ng isang 32-qubit circuit na"
" sinample na may 10,000 shot. Pagkatapos magawa ang count data, ang "
"`recover_configurations()` method ay nangangailangan na i-convert mo ang "
"count data sa isang matrix ng mga bitstring na sinukat sa bawat shot, pati "
"na rin ang isang array ng mga probability para sa bawat estado na nasukat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The artificial generation of samples is only used as a means to demonstrate the tooling of `qiskit-addon-sqd`. The package is meant to be used as part of a larger workflow wherein an ansatz or other circuit is defined, optimized, and executed using the Sampler primitive. The code cell below contains commented-out code demonstrating what a typical workflow might look like given a circuit ansatz transpiled to an ISA circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang artipisyal na pagbuo ng mga sample ay ginagamit lamang bilang paraan upang ipakita ang mga kasangkapan ng `qiskit-addon-sqd`. Ang package ay nilayon na gamitin bilang bahagi ng isang mas malaking workflow kung saan ang isang ansatz o ibang circuit ay tinutukoy, ino-optimize, at pinapatupad gamit ang Sampler primitive. Ang code cell sa ibaba ay naglalaman ng naka-comment-out na code na nagpapakita kung ano ang magiging hitsura ng isang tipikal na workflow kung binigyan ng isang circuit ansatz na na-transpile sa isang ISA circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run configuration recovery loop {#run-configuration-recovery-loop}"
msgstr ""
"Patakbuhin ang configuration recovery loop {#run-configuration-recovery-"
"loop}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The measurement samples can then be refined by repeating the configuration "
"recovery and diagonalizing sets of subsamples to approximate the ground "
"state until convergence.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga measurement sample ay maaaring pagandahin sa pamamagitan ng pag-"
"uulit ng configuration recovery at pag-diagonalize ng mga hanay ng subsample"
" upang ma-approximate ang ground state hanggang sa convergence.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, specify the following options:\n"
msgstr "Una, tukuyin ang mga sumusunod na opsyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ITERATIONS`: The number of self-consistent configuration recovery "
"iterations\n"
msgstr ""
"`ITERATIONS`: Ang bilang ng self-consistent na configuration recovery "
"iteration\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`NUM_BATCHES`: The number of sets of subsamples to diagonalize\n"
msgstr "`NUM_BATCHES`: Ang bilang ng mga hanay ng subsample na i-diagonalize\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`SAMPLES_PER_BATCH`: The number of samples to include in each batch\n"
msgstr ""
"`SAMPLES_PER_BATCH`: Ang bilang ng mga sample na isasama sa bawat batch\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MAX_DAVIDSON_CYCLES`: The number of iterations for the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr ""
"`MAX_DAVIDSON_CYCLES`: Ang bilang ng mga iteration para sa eigenstate "
"solver\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an optional step, you can define a callback function to log the details "
"for each configuration recovery iteration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang opsyonal na hakbang, maaari kang magtukoy ng callback function upang "
"i-log ang mga detalye para sa bawat configuration recovery iteration.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, run the configuration recovery loop. Each loop consists of three "
"steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, patakbuhin ang configuration recovery loop. Ang bawat loop ay "
"binubuo ng tatlong hakbang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `recover_configurations()` function to obtain a refined bitstring "
"matrix and probability array based on the average orbital occupancy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang `recover_configurations()` function upang makakuha ng refined na"
" bitstring matrix at probability array batay sa average orbital occupancy.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `postselect_and_subsample()` to collect batches of subsamples to "
"diagonalize over.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang `postselect_and_subsample()` upang mangolekta ng mga batch ng "
"subsample na i-diagonalize.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then use the batches of subsamples as arguments to the `solve_fermion()` "
"function to obtain an approximation of the ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos ay gamitin ang mga batch ng subsample bilang mga argumento sa "
"`solve_fermion()` function upang makakuha ng approximation ng ground "
"state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is important to note how to address the first iteration of the "
"configuration recovery loop. Since the average orbital occupancy is not yet "
"available, only the `postselect_and_subsample()` function is called. This "
"removes any non-physical samples (samples with incorrect Hamming weight) "
"before running the eigenstate solver, `solve_fermion()`. Afterward, the "
"average orbital occupation is calculated across all batches and used as "
"input to the `recover_configurations()` method, which flips individual bits "
"probabilistically based on this average. See Section **II-A** of the "
"supplementary information in the [SQD "
"paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalagang tandaan kung paano haharapin ang unang iteration ng configuration"
" recovery loop. Dahil hindi pa available ang average orbital occupancy, ang "
"`postselect_and_subsample()` function lamang ang tinatawag. Tinatanggal nito"
" ang anumang hindi pisikal na mga sample (mga sample na may maling Hamming "
"weight) bago patakbuhin ang eigenstate solver, `solve_fermion()`. Pagkatapos"
" nito, ang average orbital occupation ay kinakalkula sa lahat ng batch at "
"ginagamit bilang input sa `recover_configurations()` method, na nagpi-flip "
"ng mga indibidwal na bit nang probabilistically batay sa average na ito. "
"Tingnan ang Seksyon **II-A** ng supplementary information sa [SQD "
"paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the results {#visualize-the-results}"
msgstr "I-visualize ang mga resulta {#visualize-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lastly, the results can be visualized by examining the approximated energy "
"and average orbital occupancy at each iteration of the configuration "
"recovery loop. The first plot shows that after a few iterations, the ground "
"state energy is estimated to within approximately `27 mH` (chemical accuracy"
" is typically accepted to be `1 kcal/mol` $\\approx$ `1.6 mH`). Recall that "
"this demonstration used pure noise, and that the ability to approximate the "
"energy to this degree comes from prior knowledge about the molecule and its "
"electronic structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Panghuli, ang mga resulta ay maaaring i-visualize sa pamamagitan ng "
"pagsusuri sa approximated na energy at average orbital occupancy sa bawat "
"iteration ng configuration recovery loop. Ang unang plot ay nagpapakita na "
"pagkatapos ng ilang iteration, ang ground state energy ay tinatantya sa loob"
" ng humigit-kumulang `27 mH` (ang chemical accuracy ay karaniwang "
"tinatanggap na `1 kcal/mol` $\\approx$ `1.6 mH`). Tandaan na ang "
"demonstrasyon na ito ay gumamit ng purong noise, at ang kakayahang "
"i-approximate ang energy sa ganitong antas ay nagmumula sa naunang kaalaman "
"tungkol sa molecule at sa electronic structure nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second plot shows the average occupancy of each spatial orbital after "
"the final iteration. Notice that both the spin-up and spin-down electrons "
"occupy the first five orbitals with high probability in the solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangalawang plot ay nagpapakita ng average occupancy ng bawat spatial "
"orbital pagkatapos ng huling iteration. Pansinin na parehong ang spin-up at "
"spin-down na mga electron ay nag-occupy sa unang limang orbital na may "
"mataas na probability sa mga solusyon.\n"

